 "result_text": "Equation fields now use Knack's formatted value for `.formatted`, so your example should give `4` instead of `372171.318\u2026`. `.raw` still holds the raw value. I only checked that the package imports. I didn't run the tests or try a real equation field.\n\n- **`knackpy/models.py`:** I added `\"equation\": {\"use_knack_format\": True}` to `FIELD_SETTINGS`. That is the same setting `timer` and `name` fields already use.\n- **`knackpy/fields.py`:** I changed the check on the Knack-formatted value in `Field._format` from truthiness to `is not None`. Without it, a formatted value of `0` or an empty string would have fallen back to the raw value.\n\nThe second change applies to every field type that uses Knack's formatted value (`name`, `timer`, `id`), not just equations. For those, a falsy formatted value is now kept instead of replaced by the raw one.",
